n effect won't be able to be applied to any damage events.","oracle_id":"1af63a5e-2bec-4f8d-a373-d9ce43a7d242","published_at":"2019-05-03","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"More damage can be redirected to the chosen creature than it has toughness or to the chosen planeswalker than it has loyalty, as long as that damage is all dealt at once (like combat damage is) or is all dealt while a single spell or ability is resolving.","oracle_id":"1af63a5e-2bec-4f8d-a373-d9ce43a7d242","published_at":"2019-05-03","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If the chosen creature or planeswalker isn't on the battlefield or isn't a creature or planeswalker at the time damage would be dealt, the damage won't be redirected.","oracle_id":"1af63a5e-2bec-4f8d-a373-d9ce43a7d242","published_at":"2019-05-03","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Gideon's Sacrifice doesn't change the source of the damage or whether the damage is combat damage.","oracle_id":"1af63a5e-2bec-4f8d-a373-d9ce43a7d242","published_at":"2019-05-03","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Gideon's Sacrifice has no effect on damage already dealt earlier in the turn.","oracle_id":"1af63a5e-2bec-4f8d-a373-d9ce43a7d242","published_at":"2019-05-03","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If you cast more than one Gideon's Sacrifice in one turn, all damage that would be dealt at once to you and/or permanents you control is dealt to one of the chosen permanents of your choice. It's not dealt to all of them, and you can't split the damage between them. The next time damage would be dealt to you, you may choose a different one of those permanents to be dealt that damage.","oracle_id":"1af63a5e-2bec-4f8d-a373-d9ce43a7d242","published_at":"2019-05-03","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Saving Grace's ability has no effect on damage already dealt earlier in the turn.","oracle_id":"50ddbea3-7ef4-4f6a-83c9-0c3ea1dfa3c9","published_at":"2017-07-14","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"More damage can be redirected to the enchanted creature than it has toughness, as long as that damage is all dealt at once (like combat damage is).","oracle_id":"50ddbea3-7ef4-4f6a-83c9-0c3ea1dfa3c9","published_at":"2017-07-14","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If Saving Grace leaves the battlefield during the turn its triggered ability resolved, damage will continue to be redirected to the creature it enchanted before it left the battlefield. If the creature Saving Grace was last attached to isn't on the battlefield or isn't a creature at the time damage would be dealt, it won't be redirected.","oracle_id":"50ddbea3-7ef4-4f6a-83c9-0c3ea1dfa3c9","published_at":"2017-07-14","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Saving Grace's redirection effect doesn't change the source of the damage or whether the damage is combat damage.","oracle_id":"50ddbea3-7ef4-4f6a-83c9-0c3ea1dfa3c9","published_at":"2017-07-14","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If you have more than one Saving Grace enter the battlefield in one turn, all damage that would be dealt at once to you and/or permanents you control is dealt to one of the enchanted creatures of your choice. It's not dealt to all of them, and you can't split the damage between them.","oracle_id":"50ddbea3-7ef4-4f6a-83c9-0c3ea1dfa3c9","published_at":"2017-07-14","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
